IMPORT prelude

-- Ngee Ann Polytechnic Act 1967 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a student, a donor, a testator, a business contracting with
-- the Polytechnic, or a member of its Council: the size and terms of the Council and how a member's office ends (ss 7 to 9), Council
-- meetings, quorum, voting and the circulation of minutes (ss 12, 13(4), (5)), the common seal on instruments and on diplomas (s 14),
-- who votes on a committee (s 19(5)), the Ngee Ann Kongsi's gifts of land (s 20(2)), the Students' Union and the Societies Act (s 23),
-- how rules are made (s 24(1), (3)), the validation of late-payment charges (ss 24(2)(e), 24A) and old references to the Ngee Ann
-- Technical College in wills and contracts (s 25).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation ("version in force from 1/4/2024"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/NAPA1967.txt. The deposit says the revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including
-- 1 December 2021"; the latest annotation is "[Act 4 of 2008 wef 01/04/2024]" against ss 24(2)(e) and 24A. The Legislative History
-- (which says it "is not part of the Act") gives Act 4 of 2008 a commencement of 1 April 2024.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0195 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. SCOPED to the provisions such a person meets. Not encoded: incorporation and objects (ss 3, 4), the
-- Council's and Senate's lists of functions and powers (ss 6, 10, 11, 15), the Registrar's other duties (s 13(1) to (3)), the
-- Senate's composition (s 16), committees and delegation (s 17), the Principal's appointment and duties (s 19(1) to (4)), other staff
-- (s 19A), the Kongsi's other contributions (s 20(1)), shares to the Minister for Finance (s 20A), the Students' Union's constitution
-- and fee (s 22) and the list of rule-making purposes beyond late-payment charges (s 24(2)).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Ngee Ann Polytechnic Act 1967`

DECLARE `Council role` IS ONE OF
    `the Chairperson`
    `the Deputy Chairperson`
    `the Principal`
    `a Ngee Ann Kongsi representative`
    `a member the Minister determined`
    `the Registrar`
    `a Vice-Principal`

GIVEN `the role` IS A `Council role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a member of the Council` IF
    CONSIDER `the role`
    WHEN `the Registrar` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a Vice-Principal` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the role` IS A `Council role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the Principal` IF
    CONSIDER `the role`
    WHEN `the Principal` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `7 -- the Council's size and terms`

-- s 7(1): the Council is "(a) a Chairperson; (b) a Deputy Chairperson; (c) the Principal; (d) 3 representatives of the Ngee Ann Kongsi
-- nominated by its Committee of Management; and (e) not less than 6 but not more than 12 other persons as the Minister may determine."
-- (2): every member "except the Principal" is appointed by the Minister and, "unless the Minister otherwise directs, holds office for
-- a period of 3 years from the date of the appointment and is eligible for re-appointment."
-- s 9(1): a person filling a vacancy holds office "for the remainder of the term of the person's predecessor".
GIVEN `other members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the number of other members is lawful` IF
    `other members` AT LEAST 6 AND `other members` AT MOST 12

GIVEN `other members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the size of the Council` MEANS
    `other members` PLUS 6

-- The Principal sits by virtue of office and has no fixed term under s 7(2); 0 is returned for "no term under s 7(2)".
GIVEN `the member` IS A `Council role`, `fills a vacancy` IS A BOOLEAN, `predecessor's remaining years` IS A NUMBER, `the Minister directs otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN, `directed years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the term of the appointment in years` MEANS
    IF `is the Principal` `the member` THEN 0
    ELSE IF `fills a vacancy` THEN `predecessor's remaining years`
         ELSE IF `the Minister directs otherwise` THEN `directed years`
              ELSE 3

§§ `8 -- how a member's office ends`

-- s 8(1): "The office of a member of the Council is vacated if the member -- (a) becomes a bankrupt or suspends payment to, or makes
-- any arrangement or composition with, his or her creditors; or (b) has been absent, without leave of the Council, from 3 consecutive
-- meetings." Subsection (1) has no exception for the Principal; (2) and (3) do.
-- (2): the Minister may revoke the appointment of a member, "except that of the Principal", who becomes "in the opinion of the
-- Minister, unfit to continue in office or incapable of performing the member's duties".
-- (3): a member, "except the Principal, may resign ... at any time by giving written notice to the Minister."
GIVEN `became a bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN, `suspended payment or compounded with creditors` IS A BOOLEAN, `consecutive meetings missed without leave` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the office is vacated` IF
        `became a bankrupt`
    OR  `suspended payment or compounded with creditors`
    OR  `consecutive meetings missed without leave` AT LEAST 3

GIVEN `the member` IS A `Council role`, `unfit or incapable in the Minister's opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may revoke the appointment` IF
    `is a member of the Council` `the member` AND (NOT (`is the Principal` `the member`)) AND `unfit or incapable in the Minister's opinion`

GIVEN `the member` IS A `Council role`, `gave written notice to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member may resign` IF
    `is a member of the Council` `the member` AND (NOT (`is the Principal` `the member`)) AND `gave written notice to the Minister`

§§ `9 -- filling a vacancy`

-- s 9(1): "If the office of a member of the Council, other than that of the Principal, is vacant, the Minister may appoint any person
-- to fill the vacancy". (2): where the predecessor "was a representative of the Ngee Ann Kongsi, the person appointed must also be a
-- representative of the Ngee Ann Kongsi nominated by the Committee of Management."
-- s 19(1): "The Council must appoint the Principal".
DECLARE `Vacancy filler` IS ONE OF
    `any person the Minister appoints`
    `a Kongsi representative nominated by its Committee of Management`
    `not filled under section 9 -- the Council appoints the Principal`

GIVEN `the vacant seat` IS A `Council role`
GIVETH A `Vacancy filler`
`who may fill the vacancy` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the vacant seat`
    WHEN `the Principal` THEN `not filled under section 9 -- the Council appoints the Principal`
    WHEN `a Ngee Ann Kongsi representative` THEN `a Kongsi representative nominated by its Committee of Management`
    OTHERWISE `any person the Minister appoints`

§§ `12 -- Council meetings`

-- s 12(2): "The quorum at every meeting of the Council is 6 members." (3): every decision "by a simple majority of the votes of the
-- members present and voting, except that in the case of an equality of votes, the Chairperson or, in his or her absence, the Deputy
-- Chairperson of the Council has a casting vote." (5): if both are absent, "the member elected from among the members present,
-- presides" -- and the text gives that member NO casting vote. (7): a vacancy does not preclude a meeting.
GIVEN `present` IS A NUMBER, `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER, `the Chairperson or Deputy Chairperson is present` IS A BOOLEAN, `the casting vote is for` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Council resolution is carried` IF
        `present` AT LEAST 6
    AND (    `votes for` GREATER THAN `votes against`
         OR  (`votes for` EQUALS `votes against` AND `the Chairperson or Deputy Chairperson is present` AND `the casting vote is for`))

§§ `13(4), (5) -- minutes, and the secretary's vote`

-- s 13(4): "The records of any meeting must be circulated to members of the Council within 14 days of the date of the meeting."
-- (5): "The Registrar is not, unless he or she is a member of the Council appointed to serve in that capacity for a particular meeting
-- under subsection (3), entitled to vote on any question before the Council." Reading (5) as "whoever acts as secretary votes only if
-- a Council member" is an INFERENCE from its wording.
GIVEN `days after the meeting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the records were circulated in time` IF
    `days after the meeting` AT MOST 14

GIVEN `the secretary` IS A `Council role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the secretary may vote at the Council meeting` IF
    `is a member of the Council` `the secretary`

§§ `14 -- the common seal`

-- s 14(1): the seal is in the custody of the Principal and "must not be affixed to any instrument, other than a diploma or academic
-- certificate, except in the presence of the Chairperson or a member of the Council and the Principal, who must sign their names to
-- the instrument ... and the signing is sufficient evidence that the common seal ... has been duly and properly affixed".
-- (2): the seal "may be affixed to any diploma or academic certificate in the presence of any 2 officers of the Polytechnic duly
-- authorised by the Council to act in that behalf, who must sign their names".
-- That the second signer under (1) must be someone OTHER than the Principal is an INFERENCE from "and the Principal".
-- Whether a diploma may also be sealed by the (1) route is not encoded: (1) does not restrict diplomas and (2) is permissive.
GIVEN `the Principal was present and signed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the other signer` IS A `Council role`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instrument is duly sealed` IF
        `the Principal was present and signed`
    AND `is a member of the Council` `the other signer`
    AND (NOT (`is the Principal` `the other signer`))

GIVEN `authorised officers present who signed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the diploma is duly sealed` IF
    `authorised officers present who signed` AT LEAST 2

§§ `19(5) -- the Principal on committees`

-- s 19(5): "The Principal is entitled to speak at any meeting of any committee or board appointed under section 17(1), but is not
-- entitled to vote unless the Principal is a member of the committee or board."
GIVEN `the Principal is a member of the committee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Principal may vote on the committee` IF
    `the Principal is a member of the committee`

§§ `20(2) -- the Ngee Ann Kongsi's gifts of land`

-- s 20(1)(b): the Polytechnic's property includes "such immovable property as the Ngee Ann Kongsi may alienate or donate to the
-- Polytechnic". (2): "Section 20 of the Ngee Ann Kongsi (Incorporation) Ordinance 1933 does not apply to the alienation or donation of
-- immovable property by the Ngee Ann Kongsi to the Polytechnic." What section 20 of the Ordinance requires is not in the deposit.
GIVEN `the giver is the Ngee Ann Kongsi` IS A BOOLEAN, `the property is immovable` IS A BOOLEAN, `the recipient is the Polytechnic` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 20 of the Kongsi Ordinance is disapplied` IF
    `the giver is the Ngee Ann Kongsi` AND `the property is immovable` AND `the recipient is the Polytechnic`

§§ `23 -- the Students' Union and the Societies Act`

-- s 23(1): "Despite anything to the contrary in the Societies Act 1966, the provisions of that Act apply to the Ngee Ann Polytechnic
-- Students' Union and its constituent bodies". (2): the Minister for societies may by order in the Gazette exempt the Union or a
-- constituent body "from all or any of the provisions of the Societies Act 1966 subject to any conditions specified in the order."
GIVEN `exempted from the provision by Gazette order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Societies Act provision binds the Students' Union` IF
    NOT `exempted from the provision by Gazette order`

§§ `24(1), (3) -- how rules are made`

-- s 24(1): "The Council may, with the approval of the Minister, make any rules". (3): "All rules made under this section must be
-- published in the Gazette." Whether a rule not published is invalid is not said; this predicate only records the two requirements.
GIVEN `made by the Council` IS A BOOLEAN, `approved by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN, `published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rule meets the section 24 requirements` IF
    `made by the Council` AND `approved by the Minister` AND `published in the Gazette`

§§ `24(2)(e) and 24A -- late-payment charges`

-- s 24(2)(e): rules may provide for "the fees to be charged for courses of study and any other fees or charges ... including charges
-- for the late payment of any such fee or charge" [Act 4 of 2008 wef 01/04/2024].
-- s 24A: "Every amount collected before the date of commencement of the Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2008 as, or
-- purportedly as, a charge for the late payment of any fee or charge referred to in section 24(2)(e) shall be deemed to be and always
-- to have been validly collected, and no legal proceedings shall lie ... in respect of any such collection."
-- The commencement date, 1 April 2024, is taken from the annotation and the Legislative History (item 14). Dates are YYYYMMDD numbers.
GIVEN `collected as a late-payment charge` IS A BOOLEAN, `date collected` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `proceedings over the collection are barred` IF
    `collected as a late-payment charge` AND `date collected` LESS THAN 20240401

§§ `25 -- old names in wills and contracts`

-- s 25: "On and after 16 April 1982, any reference to the Ngee Ann Technical College contained in any contract, agreement, bequest,
-- will, trust or other instrument has effect as if it were a reference to the Ngee Ann Polytechnic."
-- The Legislative History notes the Act was first the "Ngee Ann College Act, 1967", renamed the Ngee Ann Technical College Act by Act
-- 17 of 1970. Section 25 says nothing about references to the "Ngee Ann College"; this predicate leaves such a reference as written.
DECLARE `Institution name` IS ONE OF
    `the Ngee Ann College`
    `the Ngee Ann Technical College`
    `the Ngee Ann Polytechnic`

GIVEN `the name in the instrument` IS A `Institution name`, `the date it takes effect` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Institution name`
`the institution the reference is read as` MEANS
    IF `the date it takes effect` AT LEAST 19820416
    THEN CONSIDER `the name in the instrument`
         WHEN `the Ngee Ann Technical College` THEN `the Ngee Ann Polytechnic`
         OTHERWISE `the name in the instrument`
    ELSE `the name in the instrument`
